Annotation(dcterms:description "A lightweight ontology for the consistent identification and description of human cohorts across EMBL-EBI resources. Each cohort is represented as a named individual with a stable identifier and minimal metadata: a definition, synonyms, the locations where its data were collected, its relations to sub-cohorts and cohort aggregations, and example studies from EMBL-EBI resources such as the GWAS Catalog, EGA, MetaboLights and PRIDE. This enables linkage, discovery and integration of cohort-related data while supporting both named and implicitly defined cohorts.")
Annotation(dcterms:license <http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0>)
Annotation(dcterms:title "Cohort Ontology")
Annotation(doap:bug-database <https://github.com/EBISPOT/cohort-ontology/issues>)
Annotation(foaf:homepage <https://github.com/EBISPOT/cohort-ontology>)

